On the wider screen, the box's middle was drawn on from its label's
ends (columns 27 and 228), which are rounded: a pixel shorter at the top
and the bottom. Drawn on from columns 28 and 227 instead, the label is
one height across; its rounded ends stay at the widened box's ends.
---
 src/applications/pokedex/ov21_021E8D48.c | 14 +++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/applications/pokedex/ov21_021E8D48.c b/src/applications/pokedex/ov21_021E8D48.c
index 6eaad902..899e59cd 100644
--- a/src/applications/pokedex/ov21_021E8D48.c
+++ b/src/applications/pokedex/ov21_021E8D48.c
@@ -68,11 +68,15 @@ static const short sPokedexRegisterWideLayout[][8] = {
     WIDE_MOVE(WIDE_BG(3), 190, 192, 248, 256, 16),
     WIDE_MOVE(WIDE_BG(3), 190, 192, 248, 256, 24),
     WIDE_MOVE(WIDE_BG(3), 190, 192, 248, 256, 32),
-    WIDE_MOVE(WIDE_BG(3), 130, 190, 27, 229, 0),
-    WIDE_MOVE(WIDE_BG(3), 130, 190, 0, 27, -32),
-    WIDE_FILL(WIDE_BG(3), 130, 190, -5, 27, 27),
-    WIDE_MOVE(WIDE_BG(3), 130, 190, 229, 256, 32),
-    WIDE_FILL(WIDE_BG(3), 130, 190, 229, 261, 228),
+    // (2026-10-27) the white label's rounded ends (columns 27 and 228, a
+    // pixel shorter at the top and bottom) kept at the widened box's ends:
+    // its middle drawn on from columns 28 and 227 (full height), so the
+    // label is one even height across
+    WIDE_MOVE(WIDE_BG(3), 130, 190, 28, 228, 0),
+    WIDE_MOVE(WIDE_BG(3), 130, 190, 0, 28, -32),
+    WIDE_FILL(WIDE_BG(3), 130, 190, -4, 28, 28),
+    WIDE_MOVE(WIDE_BG(3), 130, 190, 228, 256, 32),
+    WIDE_FILL(WIDE_BG(3), 130, 190, 228, 260, 227),
     // (2026-10-25) the Pokémon's picture frame (columns 4-91) 24 pixels to
     // the left (the pattern behind it 8 pixels wide: still in step), the
     // Pokémon (the 3D) with it; where it was, the pattern (the screen's
